    {
      "text": "knock, and it shall be opened unto you, Matt. 7:7 (3 Ne. 14:7). learn of me … and ye shall find rest unto your souls, Matt. 11:29. learn a parable of the fig tree, Matt. 24:32 (Mark 13:28; D&C 35:16; JS—M 1:38). Search the scriptures, John 5:39. learned of the Father, cometh unto me, John 6:45. Spirit of truth … will guide you into all truth, John 16:13. Moses was learned in all the wisdom, Acts 7:22. natural man receiveth not the things of the Spirit, 1 Cor. 2:14. Beware lest any man spoil you through philosophy, Col. 2:8. woman learn in silence with all subjection, 1 Tim. 2:11. let them learn first to shew piety at home, 1 Tim. 5:4. withal they learn to be idle, 1 Tim. 5:13. Ever learning, and never able to come to the knowledge, 2 Tim. 3:7. learn to maintain good works, Titus 3:14. Though he were a Son, yet learned he obedience, Heb. 5:8. add to your faith virtue; and to virtue knowledge, 2 Pet. 1:5.",
