    {
      "text": "taught somewhat in all the learning of my father, 1 Ne. 1:1. scriptures … might be for our profit and learning, 1 Ne. 19:23. I speak … for your profit and learning, 2 Ne. 2:14. writeth them for the learning and the profit of my children, 2 Ne. 4:15. to be learned is good if they hearken, 2 Ne. 9:29. who are puffed up because of their learning, 2 Ne. 9:42. preach up … their own wisdom and their own learning, 2 Ne. 26:20. he was learned, that he had a perfect knowledge, Jacob 7:4. neither was the teacher any better than the learner, Alma 1:26. lawyers were learned in all the arts, Alma 10:15. not harden his heart, to him is given the greater portion, Alma 12:10. ye may learn wisdom, Alma 32:12. learn wisdom in thy youth, Alma 37:35. learn of me that there is no other way, Alma 38:9. receive great learning because of their riches, 3 Ne. 6:12. ye may learn to be more wise than we have been, Morm. 9:31.",
