      "text": "Learn of me … and you shall have peace in me, D&C 19:23. he that receiveth light, and continueth in God, receiveth more, D&C 50:24. seek learning, even by study and also by faith, D&C 88:118 (109:7). learn to impart one to another, D&C 88:123. study and learn … books … languages, tongues, D&C 90:15. chastened until they learn obedience, D&C 105:6 (105:3). let every man learn his duty, and to act in the office, D&C 107:99. they do not learn this one lesson, D&C 121:35 (121:39). Whatever … intelligence we attain unto in this life, it will rise with us, D&C 130:18. impossible for a man to be saved in ignorance, D&C 131:6. Let him that is ignorant learn wisdom by humbling, D&C 136:32. their first lessons in the world of spirits, D&C 138:56.",
